{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Buggy Auto-Fix Loop",
  "description": "After Kiro finishes any coding task, automatically run Buggy analysis on changed files. If bugs are found, investigate them and PRESENT any approved fixes (diff + overfitting score) for the developer to review. Nothing is applied without the developer's explicit choice.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "agentStop"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "The agent just finished a coding task. Now perform a proof-carrying bug REVIEW — do NOT edit any code automatically:\n\n1. Identify which .ts files were modified in this session (check git diff or recent file edits).\n2. For each modified file, call buggy_analyze to check for issues.\n3. If issues are found, call buggy_list_functions to identify the affected functions.\n4. For each risky function (division, array access without bounds, unclamped operations), call buggy_investigate with inferred preconditions and postconditions.\n5. For each proven bug, PRESENT it to the developer: the function, the trigger input, the violated rule, and — for every approved patch — its diff and overfitting score (lowest first). Do not apply anything yet.\n6. Ask the developer which fix (if any) to apply. Only apply the specific patch they choose, using str_replace, then re-run buggy_analyze on that file to confirm it is clean.\n7. Stop after presenting all findings, or once the developer has decided.\n\nKeep it concise. For each finding: \"[function] — [bug] (trigger X). Approved fix, overfitting Y%: [show diff] — apply it?\" If no bugs are found, say nothing."
  }
}